# Adaptive EO/IR Sensor Selection Algorithm

This project implements an adaptive decision algorithm in MATLAB/Simulink for selecting between EO (visible-spectrum) and IR sensors based on environmental conditions and sensor health.

The algorithm continuously calculates a performance score for each sensor and switches to the more suitable channel when required.

## Inputs

- Ambient illumination (lux)
- Visibility
- EO scene contrast
- Thermal contrast (ΔT)
- EO sensor health
- IR sensor health
- AUTO / MANUAL operating mode

## Operating Modes

### AUTO Mode
The algorithm automatically selects the most suitable sensor according to the calculated EO and IR performance scores.

### MANUAL Mode
The operator can force either EO or IR selection. If the selected sensor becomes unavailable, the algorithm can fall back to the healthy sensor.

## Main Features

- EO and IR performance scoring
- Automatic sensor selection
- Hysteresis to prevent unnecessary switching
- Transition confirmation time
- Automatic sensor failover
- Dual-sensor fault detection
- Active sensor confidence calculation
- Operational / degraded / fault status

## Outputs

- Active Sensor
- EO Performance Score
- IR Performance Score
- Sensor Confidence
- Payload Status

This model demonstrates a simplified EO/IR sensor management algorithm for electro-optical payload applications.
